# Claude Code Configuration for Claudex Repository

# Git Commit Configuration
# IMPORTANT: Never add co-author attribution to commits in this repository
# All commits should be attributed to the primary author only

# This prevents the following lines from being added to commit messages:
# - "🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](...)"
# - "Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"

# To ensure this setting is respected:
# 1. Do not use git commit templates that add co-author lines
# 2. All commits should be clean without additional attribution footers
# 3. If co-author lines are accidentally added, use git filter-branch to remove them:
#    git filter-branch -f --msg-filter 'sed "/🤖 Generated with/d" | sed "/Co-Authored-By: Claude/d"' -- --all
#    git push --force origin main
